=== D.1 ROBUSTNESS TO THE SLIDE-6 CHECK ===

The thesis reports the tick rates in Table 3.2 but never uses them. For
popularity the rate is 60.5% overall and 55.9% in the M2 subsample, not
distinguishable from the 50% expected by chance (p = 0.18).
CAUTION: slide 6 is not a perception check. It is a single multiple-choice
question asked at the end about which cues the respondent SAYS they used, so
it is post-treatment and plausibly affected by the treatment itself.
What follows describes how fragile the popularity null is; it does not
overturn it. See docs/01-review-of-2023-work.md section 3.3.

